        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "For one wall in an 8\u00d710 room, it depends on which wall and how tall it is.\n\nA 12-inch square covers **1 square foot**.\n\nSo:\n\n- an **8-foot-wide wall** needs **8 tiles per foot of height**\n- a **10-foot-wide wall** needs **10 tiles per foot of height**\n\nExamples:\n\n- **8 ft wide \u00d7 8 ft tall wall** = **64** 12-inch squares\n- **10 ft wide \u00d7 8 ft tall wall** = **80** 12-inch squares\n\nIf you want to cover **all 4 walls** of an 8\u00d710 room with **8-foot ceilings**:\n- Perimeter = 8 + 10 + 8 + 10 = **36 feet**\n- 36 \u00d7 8 = **288** squares\n\nTell me your wall height and whether you mean **one wall or the whole room**, and I\u2019ll give you the exact number."
          ]
        },
